## Read-Only Domain Controllers (RODCs)

RODCs provide a specialized deployment option designed for branch offices and other locations with limited physical security.

### RODC Characteristics

**Read-only NTDS.dit** means RODCs cannot make changes to the directory, only serve authentication requests from their cached copy.

**Limited password replication** restricts which accounts have passwords cached locally, reducing the exposure if the RODC is compromised.

**Different krbtgt account** creates a separate Kerberos service account, limiting the blast radius of RODC compromise.

**Designed for branch offices** where physical security may be insufficient for traditional Domain Controllers.

### RODC Security Benefits

| Traditional DC | RODC |
|----------------|------|
| Compromised DC = Domain compromise | Compromised RODC ≠ Domain compromise |
| Full credential exposure | Can be "disowned" if stolen |
| Complete replication rights | Limited credential exposure |

