## The krbtgt Account: Special Attention Required

<div class="crown-jewels" markdown="1">
**What Makes krbtgt Special?**

- Used to sign ALL Kerberos tickets
- Password never expires automatically
- Created when domain is built
- Same password might be 10+ years old!
</div>

### krbtgt Security Implications

```
Old krbtgt password + Previous admin/backup = Permanent backdoor
```

**Best Practices for krbtgt Management:**

**Rotate krbtgt password periodically** to invalidate any compromised tickets and prevent Golden Ticket attacks.

**Must rotate TWICE** due to password history requirements that maintain the previous password for compatibility.

**Wait 10+ hours between rotations** to ensure proper replication and prevent authentication failures.

**Monitor for Golden Ticket attacks** by watching for unusual Kerberos ticket requests and impossible authentication scenarios.

