## Domain Controller Backup & Recovery

### Critical Backup Components

**System State backups** include the NTDS.dit database along with registry settings and other system components necessary for Domain Controller restoration.

**SYSVOL backups** preserve Group Policy Objects and logon scripts that define domain-wide configurations.

**Full Server Backup** enables bare metal recovery in catastrophic failure scenarios.

### Backup Security

Backup security requires special attention due to the sensitive nature of Domain Controller data:

**Encrypted backups** protect password hashes and other sensitive information contained within the NTDS.dit database.

**Secure storage** implements both physical and logical access controls to prevent unauthorized backup access.

**Offsite copies** provide disaster recovery capabilities while maintaining appropriate security controls.

**Test restores** in isolated environments verify backup integrity without exposing production systems.

<div class="key-concept" markdown="1">
**DSRM (Directory Services Restore Mode):** Local "break glass" administrator account that can be abused if registry settings are modified by attackers.
</div>

