## Common DC Vulnerabilities

### 1. Print Spooler (PrintNightmare)

<div class="vulnerability-alert" markdown="1">
**Issue:** Enabled by default on Domain Controllers
**Risk:** Multiple critical vulnerabilities enabling privilege escalation
**Fix:** Disable Print Spooler service on all Domain Controllers
</div>

### 2. Zerologon (CVE-2020-1472)

<div class="vulnerability-alert" markdown="1">
**Issue:** Netlogon protocol cryptographic vulnerability
**Risk:** Instant Domain Controller compromise with no credentials
**Fix:** Apply security patches immediately and monitor for exploitation attempts
</div>

### 3. PetitPotam & Weak Backups

<div class="vulnerability-alert" markdown="1">
**PetitPotam:** Forces authentication via EFSRPC for NTLM relay attacks
**Fix:** Disable EFS service or apply patches and implement EPA

**Weak Backup Security:** Backup files accessible to non-administrators
**Fix:** Implement proper backup infrastructure security controls
</div>

